{
 "id": "p2-w10-m5",
 "title": "Encrypted is not the same as safe",
 "alt": "A whiteboard sketch contrasting a properly authenticated TLS connection, drawn as a locked tube between client and server carrying confidentiality, integrity and authentication, with the same picture under verify=False where an attacker is spliced into the middle holding two perfectly good tunnels and the client's lock is crossed out in red; below it the chain of trust from root CA to intermediate to leaf with a self-signed certificate crossed out, a to-scale comparison of a 53 millisecond TLS 1.2 handshake against a 32.5 millisecond TLS 1.3 handshake and a zero-RTT stub marked replayable, and a reverse proxy box annotated with the three things it changes.",
 "width": 1000,
 "height": 790,
 "tier": "T2",
 "week": 10,
